From 0d4c5bd87390c802a8a3f302deb1fb49bce49779 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:46:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09170/11362] Make the loop drive itself: sweep every boolean
 capability flag, refuse the rest

REQ-ARC-FLAG-SWEEP-6271. The selection machinery existed but a human had to point
it at one flag at a time, which is not unattended self-improvement. `--sweep`
measures every unmeasured boolean capability flag on an engine and promotes what
earns it.

WHAT IT WILL NOT TOUCH, and this is the substance of the change. Of the 54
default-off flags the scored engine reaches, only 20 are boolean capability
toggles. A sweep that set every one to "1" would set `CARNOT_ARC_GGUF_PATH` to a
nonsense model path, `CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TIMEOUT` to a one-second timeout that
breaks induction outright, and `CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_INDUCTION` to on -- turning
the LLM OFF -- then watch the numbers fall and record the damage as evidence that
those capabilities are harmful. A ledger full of confident wrong verdicts is worse
than an empty one.

`classify_flag` reads how each value is USED at its `environ.get` site and returns
bool / numeric / path / inverse / guard / unknown. Only `bool` is swept.

  bool      20   measured
  unknown   54   NOT measured -- some are plainly numeric on inspection
                 (GOAL_GATE_MAX_NODES, GENERATOR_SEED); under-sweeping costs
                 coverage, over-sweeping costs correctness
  numeric    6   "=1" is a value, not an enable
  path       5   "=1" is not a path
  guard      2   see below
  inverse    1   DISABLE_* -- turning it on REMOVES a capability

The `guard` class exists because of `CARNOT_ARC_E3_ALLOW_EVIDENCE_WRITE`, which
disables the protection stopping tests from writing the TRACKED e3 evidence
directory. It is inert outside pytest, so sweeping it yields a confident
meaningless null -- and its name sitting in a list called "capability flags"
would tell the next reader it had been measured and found worthless. After a day
spent restoring artifacts a test run rewrote, a sweep should not be in the habit
of flipping write-permission flags at all.

Every exclusion is printed with its reason. A sweep that quietly shrinks its own
candidate list is this project's signature bug with a progress bar.

ONE SHARED BASELINE. Per-flag measurement runs baseline+arm, so 20 flags is 40
sweeps. The search is deterministic -- dc22 spent exactly 11,737 actions on two
separate runs -- so the baseline is computed once and reused: 21 sweeps, not 40.
The halving follows from the determinism rather than working around it, and if a
stochastic component is ever added to the search this optimisation becomes wrong
and the per-flag baseline must return. Resumable: a flag with recorded evidence is
skipped, so an interrupted six-hour run continues instead of restarting.

Also fixes a real quadratic found by the tests hanging: `classify_flag` re-read
the whole agent tree per flag, roughly 19,000 file reads across 95 flags, slow
enough that listing candidates looked like a hang. Sources are now read once.

43 tests.

